00:05:47,759 --> 00:05:51,659
Another question I got was how you're meant to play scout on narrow maps like Dust Bowl.

54
00:05:52,019 --> 00:05:56,419
Honestly, maps like Dust Bowl and Gold Rush are where you need to take all of this advice the most seriously.

55
00:05:56,699 --> 00:06:01,719
They're old restrictive maps where the balance has aged pretty badly, especially for red.

56
00:06:01,719 --> 00:06:06,899
Your respawn can be anywhere from 18 to 22 seconds and the points can be captured absurdly quickly.

57
00:06:06,899 --> 00:06:11,919
And because of that, there isn't some secret flank or defensive strategy that suddenly makes Scout amazing.

58
00:06:11,919 --> 00:06:14,899
You have to be extremely deliberate about where you position yourself,

59
00:06:14,899 --> 00:06:18,199
which fights you take, and whether you are actually where your team needs you.

60
00:06:18,339 --> 00:06:21,819
High ground is still important, but only if it's actually safe.

61
00:06:21,899 --> 00:06:26,719
Most of the obvious high ground on the first section of Dust Bowl leaves you exposed to snipers and spam.

62
00:06:27,099 --> 00:06:29,599
Sometimes you genuinely have to play around the point and

63
00:06:29,599 --> 00:06:33,039
and be prepared to back up once your team loses that space.

64
00:06:33,039 --> 00:06:36,639
In this clip, I move around and I help my team defend the choke,

65
00:06:36,639 --> 00:06:39,599
